I interpret a bare letteral (or ko'a etc.) which has not been defined (expl=
icitly with {goi} or by using the word it stands for in full) as I interpre=
t a "he" or "it" or "she" in English which has no (context-)defined referen=
t. It's grammatical but kind of a placeholder.

>I disagree with iesk that we would ever assume it is standing in for a ini=
